# Files the credential scanner may skip, and WHY.
#
# An allowlist is a hole by construction, so every entry carries its
# justification and anything not listed here is a hard failure. If you are
# adding a line, the burden is on you to show the string cannot authenticate
# anything.

# The scanner itself. Its pattern list literally contains the prefixes it hunts
# for, so it matches itself. Same shape as the bug in DECISIONS 010, where the
# staged-diff scanner blocked its own introducing commit.
scripts/precommit.sh

# Deliberate NEGATIVE fixtures. These assert that the environment layer REFUSES
# a live key at boot, which is the control that keeps an automatic fail
# impossible. "sk_live_abc123" is not a key; it is the input to a test that
# proves we reject keys of that shape. Deleting it would remove the proof.
src/lib/__tests__/env.test.ts

